%% Source-backed Fallback sequence
sequenceDiagram
    actor RequesterOp as Requester KDKMP Operator
    actor RequesterMgr as Requester KDKMP Manager
    actor SupplierOp as NETWORK KDKMP Operator
    actor SupplierMgr as NETWORK KDKMP Manager
    participant UI as React/Inertia UI
    participant Route as routes/web.php + role middleware
    participant ReqC as FallbackRequestController / Action / Approval
    participant OfferC as FallbackOfferController / Action / Review / Incoming
    participant ReqS as FallbackRequestService
    participant OfferS as FallbackOfferService
    participant Reserve as FallbackReservationService
    participant Metrics as SupplyMetricsService
    participant Support as Audit / OperationalNotification
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    RequesterOp->>UI: Create Fallback Request from current Shortfall
    UI->>Route: POST /kdkmp/fallback-requests
    Route->>ReqC: store()
    ReqC->>ReqS: createDraft request command
    ReqS->>DB: transaction + lock Forecast
    ReqS->>Metrics: calculate current Shortfall
    Metrics->>DB: read canonical supply state
    ReqS->>DB: INSERT fallback_requests (DRAFT)
    ReqS->>Support: audit

    RequesterOp->>UI: Submit Request
    UI->>Route: POST /kdkmp/fallback-requests/{request}/submit
    Route->>ReqC: FallbackRequestActionController::submit()
    ReqC->>ReqS: submit request command
    ReqS->>DB: lock Request + Forecast; revalidate Shortfall/deadline
    ReqS->>DB: UPDATE Request -> PENDING_APPROVAL
    ReqS->>Support: notify requester Manager

    RequesterMgr->>UI: Approve broadcast
    UI->>Route: POST /kdkmp/manager/fallback-requests/{request}/approve
    Route->>ReqC: FallbackRequestApprovalController::approve()
    ReqC->>ReqS: approveBroadcast command
    ReqS->>DB: lock Request + Forecast; maker-checker + revalidation
    ReqS->>DB: UPDATE Request -> OPEN
    ReqS->>Support: notify eligible NETWORK organizations after commit

    SupplierOp->>UI: Open Fallback Network and prepare source-backed Offer
    UI->>Route: POST /kdkmp/fallback-network/{request}/offers
    Route->>OfferC: FallbackOfferController::store()
    OfferC->>OfferS: createDraft source-backed offer command
    OfferS->>DB: validate supplier NETWORK membership and source commitments
    OfferS->>DB: INSERT fallback_offers + fallback_offer_sources (DRAFT)

    SupplierOp->>UI: Submit Offer
    UI->>Route: POST /kdkmp/fallback-offers/{offer}/submit
    Route->>OfferC: FallbackOfferActionController::submit()
    OfferC->>OfferS: submit offer command
    OfferS->>DB: UPDATE Offer -> PENDING_APPROVAL

    SupplierMgr->>UI: Approve outgoing Offer
    UI->>Route: POST /kdkmp/manager/outgoing-offers/{offer}/approve
    Route->>OfferC: FallbackOfferReviewController::approve()
    OfferC->>OfferS: approveForAvailability command
    OfferS->>DB: lock Offer + Request + source commitments
    OfferS->>Reserve: reserve eligible source capacity
    Reserve->>DB: UPDATE fallback_offer_sources reserved_volume atomically
    Reserve-->>OfferS: reservation successful
    OfferS->>DB: UPDATE Offer -> AVAILABLE
    OfferS->>Support: notify requester Manager

    RequesterMgr->>UI: Accept available Offer
    UI->>Route: POST /kdkmp/manager/incoming-offers/{offer}/accept
    Route->>OfferC: IncomingFallbackOfferController::accept()
    OfferC->>OfferS: accept command
    OfferS->>DB: lock Offer + Request + source commitments
    OfferS->>Metrics: calculate request remaining volume / current source validity
    OfferS->>Reserve: allocate accepted volume; release unused reserve
    Reserve->>DB: UPDATE allocated_volume + released_volume
    OfferS->>DB: UPDATE Offer -> ACCEPTED
    OfferS->>DB: UPDATE Request -> FULFILLED when requested volume is met
    OfferS->>Support: audit + notifications + derived observation

    OfferS->>Metrics: recalculate canonical supply state after acceptance
    Metrics->>DB: include only ACCEPTED fallback volume whose source remains valid
    Metrics-->>OfferS: updated Safe Supply / Shortfall / contributors
    OfferS-->>UI: redirect / response; subsequent Inertia reads use recalculated state
